#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Hicks Decomposition in Practice]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Separates price change effects on consumer behavior 🛍️]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Substitution effect: change in consumption due to price change 💰]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Income effect: change in consumption due to real income change 💸]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("Hicks Decomposition is a powerful tool in economics that helps separate the effects of a price change on consumer behavior into two components: the substitution effect and the income effect.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("The substitution effect shows how consumption changes when the price changes, keeping utility constant. It represents the change in the optimal consumption bundle due to the change in relative prices.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("The income effect, on the other hand, shows how consumption changes due to a change in real income after adjusting for the substitution effect. It represents the change in the optimal consumption bundle due to the change in purchasing power.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Applications in Economics]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Analyzing consumer response to price changes 📈]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Predicting demand shifts due to taxes or subsidies 🏛️]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Understanding welfare effects of price changes 🌍]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("Hicks Decomposition has several practical applications in economics. It allows economists to analyze how consumers respond to price changes by separating the substitution and income effects.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("This decomposition can be used to predict how demand for a good will shift when taxes or subsidies are imposed, as these policies effectively change the price faced by consumers.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("Moreover, Hicks Decomposition helps in understanding the welfare effects of price changes. By separating the substitution and income effects, it provides insights into how price changes affect consumer well-being.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Consumer Behavior Analysis]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Identifying consumer preferences and trade-offs 🤔]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Designing effective pricing strategies 💡]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Segmenting markets based on price sensitivity 🎯]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("In the realm of consumer behavior analysis, Hicks Decomposition is instrumental in identifying consumer preferences and trade-offs. By examining the substitution and income effects, marketers can gain insights into how consumers make choices between different goods.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("This understanding can be leveraged to design effective pricing strategies. By considering the relative magnitudes of the substitution and income effects, firms can set prices that optimize their profits while taking into account consumer behavior.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("Furthermore, Hicks Decomposition can be used to segment markets based on price sensitivity. Consumers with larger substitution effects are more likely to switch between goods in response to price changes, while those with larger income effects are more sensitive to changes in their purchasing power.")
]
]

